WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.439 --> 00:00:01.510
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:04.090
- [Narrator] Chinese COVID-19
vaccines are being used

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:06.080
in dozens of countries.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.043
- China has donated vaccines everywhere

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:13.037
for those countries who need help.

00:00:13.037 --> 00:00:14.540
- [Narrator] But these shots have some

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.800
of the lowest efficacy rates

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.410
among globally used coronavirus vaccines,

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.400
ranging between 50 to nearly 80%.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.400
Compare this with shots from
Pfizer-BioNTech, Moderna

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.600
and Russia's Sputnik V.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.730
The head of China CDC in
early April said the efficacy

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.710
of some vaccines was not high.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.700
And this also included
ones from his own country.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.340
So China is looking to
bolster the protection rate

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.860
and one way is to mix and match
different types of vaccines.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.600
And this idea isn't new.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.120
- We really welcome studies

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.440
that would look at mix and match regimens.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:49.420
- [Narrator] Spain is also
interested in combining vaccines

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:50.810
while researchers in the UK

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:53.570
and Russia are already studying this.

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:55.000
So as China joins the ranks

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.210
of countries looking to mix and match,

00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.190
here's how it can be a key

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:01.283
to overcoming multiple
vaccination challenges at once.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.990
Most Chinese vaccines and
other shots currently in use

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:10.110
require two doses, creating an
opportunity to mix and match.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.360
Some immunologists believe
this could have a number

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:15.120
of benefits like boosting
the immune response.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:18.390
- The theory is that if
you train the immune system

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:21.300
to recognize a virus in a
slightly different way each time,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.520
then you might get a broader

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.400
and more durable immune response.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:27.090
- [Narrator] And a more
robust immune response

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.370
is important since China
has confirmed cases

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:31.260
of new and more transmissible variants

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.450
that were first identified
in the UK and South Africa.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.850
Mixing and matching for this
reason has gotten support

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.740
from at least one Chinese
drug maker so far.

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:41.200
Some immunologists also say

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.090
that mixing and matching
could ease the pressure

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:44.810
from the vaccine supply chain.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:45.810
So for example,

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.790
in countries that are
rolling out Chinese vaccines

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.330
along with other supplies,

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.960
using two different shots
could give doctors more options

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:54.470
when patients come in for the second dose.

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:56.000
But one of the most important reasons

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.530
is when there are severe side effects

00:01:57.530 --> 00:01:59.530
from one of the vaccines.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.390
- If someone perhaps has a strange

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:03.950
or severe allergic reaction to
the first shot that they get,

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:05.820
perhaps then you could avoid that

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:09.433
by giving them the second
dose from a different vaccine.

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.520
- [Narrator] The idea became
particularly important

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.410
after regulators started investigating

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:15.920
rare blood clotting disorders linked

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.863
to AstraZeneca's COVID vaccine.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:21.220
As of late March, 79 people in the UK

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:22.570
have had severe blood clots

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:24.710
out of the 20 million administered doses

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:27.070
of AstraZeneca's vaccine.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:28.060
In France and Germany,

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.020
health authorities are
advising younger people

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.680
who have received a
first dose of AstraZeneca

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:35.570
to get a second dose
of a different vaccine.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.860
The drug maker said it's
working with health regulators

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.670
and starting the rare
blood clotting events

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:41.003
and possible causes.

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.230
While these upsides could
bring China and other countries

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:47.680
closer to getting their
population vaccinated,

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.630
health authority say
there's still a lot to learn

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:52.730
about possible side effects
or how it may affect efficacy

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.970
of the vaccines, especially when it comes

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:58.320
to combining shots made
with different technologies.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:02:59.953
- The vaccine, such as Chinese vaccine

00:02:59.953 --> 00:03:02.620
and the vaccines by AstraZeneca
and Johnson &amp; Johnson

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:04.940
are vaccines that use
a virus as the vector

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:07.890
to get the genetic
instructions into your body.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.450
- [Narrator] Whereas
Pfizer-BioNTech and Moderna vaccines

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:14.250
use a new gene-base technology
involving messenger RNA,

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.700
where molecules carry
genetic instructions.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:17.990
- So we're not too sure what happens

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:19.970
when you mix these two
technologies together.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.770
- [Narrator] Chinese health
authorities have said people

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:24.730
can receive different brands
that use the same technology,

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:26.450
but don't recommend mixing vaccines

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:29.110
with different technology so far.

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.690
But now trials with the combination

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:33.420
of two homegrown vaccines
with different technologies

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.710
are underway in China with
more than a hundred volunteers.

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:39.670
The country is also working
on its own mRNA vaccine

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:42.880
and looking closely at
approving Pfizer-BioNTech shot,

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.580
according to people
familiar with the matter.

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.850
This would pave the way
for China to mix and match

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:51.020
its more conventional
vaccines with mRNA shots.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:53.500
Similar to how researchers
in the UK are studying

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.510
the combination of AstraZeneca

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.780
with Pfizer-BioNTech or Moderna.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:00.660
Those results are expected as early as may

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:01.760
- Immunologists, when you speak to them

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.100
about this sort of process, are
pretty enthusiastic about it

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.700
and optimistic that it's going to work.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:08.140
But that's maybe the one big drawback

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:09.800
is we want to make sure that it works,

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:12.190
we want to make sure that it isn't worse,

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:13.660
you don't get a worse immune response

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:16.580
than if you had two doses
of the same vaccine.

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.163
(gentle music)

